4. Further provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), are regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 3

The objectives of protecting women and children from acts of violence are:
a. to prevent all forms of violence against women and children;
b. to provide protection and services to women and child victims of gender-based violence;
c. to provide a sense of security to women and child victims of violence;
d. to restore the physical, psychological and economic condition of women and child victims of violence;
e. the best interests of women and child victims of violence that occur in the domestic and/or public sphere; and
f. to take action against perpetrators of violence against women and children.

Article 24

1. In order to achieve the objectives of protecting women and children, cooperation may be carried out with:
a. Central Government;
b. Provincial Government;
c. Other Regency/City Governments;
d. Non-Governmental Institutions;
e. Community;
f. Universities; and.
g. Mass Media.
